# The secrets "Deploy to Cloudflare" asks for: every name in this file is shown on the deploy page
# as a secret to fill in. Keep this file to what a person deploying SHOULD type — an example value
# here can end up as the real one.
#
# SEZI_CLAIM_SECRET — your claim key (src/auth/claim.rs). Until the server is claimed, only a
# request carrying this same value gets its founding invite, and the Sezi app asks for it at the
# claim. Use a long random value (24+ characters: a password manager, or `openssl rand -base64 24`)
# and keep it until you have claimed the server. Left empty, the first visitor to the address can
# claim the server before you do.
#
# Everything else is generated by the server itself on first boot (the JWT signing key, the admin
# key), and the optional settings (TURN, push) are added later in the dashboard — see README.md.
SEZI_CLAIM_SECRET=""
